and a lot of these other agencies have been able to fund full-time clinicians to work for their departments that will actually go out 24 hours a day with officers on patrol and respond to these sorts of calls obviously we're not in a situation here where we can afford that so we we really are fortunate that the crmc and and others have teamed up to make this co-responder grant what this will do is it's going to hire two full-time clinicians at the hospital and what it does for the city it will have fifty two thousand dollars in overtime costs to pay for officers to go work out on patrol with a clinician in their car responding to these sort of calls these these clinicians also have other people that that they're working with so

